      "source": [
        "# Rebalance AI \u2014 Reinforcement Learning Based Dynamic Portfolio Optimization Using PPO\n",
        "\n",
        "**A Professional-Grade Quantitative Portfolio Management Framework**\n",
        "\n",
        "### System Overview & Resume Alignment\n",
        "> *\"Rebalance AI \u2014 Developed a PPO-based Actor-Critic reinforcement learning agent for continuous portfolio allocation across multiple financial assets. Built modular data, RL training, and backtesting pipelines, incorporating transaction costs and portfolio constraints; evaluated performance using Sharpe ratio, cumulative returns, and maximum drawdown.\"*\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook provides a complete quantitative walkthrough of the Rebalance AI system:\n",
        "1. Historical Financial Data Acquisition & Verification (`yfinance` across SPY, QQQ, TLT, GLD, EFA)\n",
        "2. Feature Engineering (Returns, Volatilities, Moving Average Ratios, RSI) & Strict Non-Look-Ahead Scaling\n",
        "3. Custom Gymnasium Trading Environment (`PortfolioEnv`) with Iterative Weight Projection & Transaction Cost Accounting\n",
        "4. Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) Actor-Critic Architecture Analysis\n",
        "5. Out-of-Sample Backtesting across 2023\u20132024 Unseen Test Data\n",
        "6. Performance Benchmarking against Equal-Weight (1/N), Buy-and-Hold, S&P 500 (SPY), and 60/40 Institutional Portfolios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set root directory\n",
        "PROJECT_ROOT = Path(\".\").resolve().parent if Path(\".\").resolve().name == \"notebooks\" else Path(\".\").resolve()\n",
        "if str(PROJECT_ROOT) not in sys.path:\n",
        "    sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n",
        "\n",
        "from config import CONFIG\n",
        "from src.data_loader import download_market_data\n",
        "from src.features import build_features\n",
        "from src.preprocessing import prepare_market_dataset\n",
        "from src.portfolio_env import PortfolioEnv, project_portfolio_weights\n",
        "from src.ppo_agent import load_ppo_agent\n",
        "from src.backtest import BacktestEngine\n",
        "from src.metrics import create_comparison_table\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
        "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (12, 6)\n",
        "print(\"Rebalance AI modules imported successfully!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Financial Market Data Collection\n",
        "\n",
        "We download and clean daily adjusted closing prices for a diversified 5-asset portfolio covering 10 years (2015 to 2025):\n",
        "- **SPY**: S&P 500 ETF (US Large-Cap Equities)\n",
        "- **QQQ**: Invesco QQQ (US Tech & Growth Equities)\n",
        "- **TLT**: 20+ Year Treasury Bond ETF (Fixed Income / Duration Hedge)\n",
        "- **GLD**: SPDR Gold Trust (Precious Metals / Inflation Hedge)\n",
        "- **EFA**: MSCI EAFE ETF (Developed International Equities)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "prices_df = download_market_data()\n",
        "print(f\"Market Data Shape: {prices_df.shape}\")\n",
        "display(prices_df.head())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Normalized asset price trajectories (rebased to $100)\n",
        "norm_prices = (prices_df / prices_df.iloc[0]) * 100.0\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "for col in norm_prices.columns:\n",
        "    plt.plot(norm_prices.index, norm_prices[col], label=f\"{col} - {CONFIG.asset.ticker_descriptions.get(col, '')}\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Asset Price Evolution (Rebased to $100 at 2015-01-02)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Normalized Price ($)\")\n",
        "plt.legend(loc=\"upper left\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Feature Engineering & Non-Look-Ahead Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "For each asset, we compute:\n",
        "1. **Returns**: 1-day, 5-day, 20-day returns and daily log returns\n",
        "2. **Volatility**: 20-day and 60-day rolling annualized standard deviation\n",
        "3. **Moving Average Trend**: Price relative to 20-day and 50-day Simple Moving Average $(P_t / \\text{SMA} - 1)$\n",
        "4. **Momentum**: 14-day Wilder's Relative Strength Index (RSI), scaled to $[0, 1]$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Strict Chronological Partitioning\n",
        "- **Train Set**: 2015-03-31 to 2021-12-31 (1,703 trading days)\n",
        "- **Validation Set**: 2022-01-03 to 2022-12-30 (251 trading days)\n",
        "- **Test Set**: 2023-01-03 to 2024-12-31 (502 trading days)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Crucial Anti-Look-Ahead Rule**: The `StandardScaler` is fitted **strictly on the training split**, and its parameters are applied forward to transform validation and test splits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "splits = prepare_market_dataset()\n",
        "print(f\"Training Split:   {len(splits.train.dates)} trading days ({splits.train.dates[0].date()} to {splits.train.dates[-1].date()})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Validation Split: {len(splits.val.dates)} trading days ({splits.val.dates[0].date()} to {splits.val.dates[-1].date()})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Testing Split:    {len(splits.test.dates)} trading days ({splits.test.dates[0].date()} to {splits.test.dates[-1].date()})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Total Engineered Features per Day: {len(splits.feature_names)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify zero look-ahead normalization\n",
        "print(f\"Train Features Mean: {splits.train.features.mean():.4f} (expected ~0.0)\")\n",
        "print(f\"Train Features Std:  {splits.train.features.std():.4f} (expected ~1.0)\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test Features Mean:  {splits.test.features.mean():.4f} (transformed with train scaler)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Custom Portfolio Environment (`PortfolioEnv`)\n",
        "\n",
        "The custom Gymnasium environment simulates daily portfolio management with:\n",
        "- **Continuous Action Scores**: The agent outputs continuous allocation scores $a \\in \\mathbb{R}^N$.\n",
        "- **Numerically Stable Softmax & Constraint Projection**: Enforces non-negativity $w_i \\ge 0$, $\\sum w_i = 1$, and single-asset concentration cap $w_i \\le 0.40$.\n",
        "- **Proportional Transaction Costs**: $\\text{Cost}_t = V_t \\cdot c_{prop} \\sum |w_{t, i}^* - w_{t, i}^-|$ deducted immediately from available capital.\n",
        "- **Exact Post-Movement Drift**: Assets drift according to daily price returns $R_{t, i}$, and next day's starting weights $w_{t+1}^-$ are computed from resulting asset values."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Verify portfolio constraint projection with an extreme test action\n",
        "extreme_action = np.array([10.0, 1.0, -2.0, 0.5, 0.0])\n",
        "projected_w = project_portfolio_weights(extreme_action, max_weight=0.40)\n",
        "print(\"Raw Action Scores:       \", extreme_action)\n",
        "print(\"Projected Weights:       \", projected_w.round(4))\n",
        "print(\"Sum of Weights:          \", np.sum(projected_w))\n",
        "print(\"All Non-Negative:        \", np.all(projected_w >= 0.0))\n",
        "print(\"Max Cap Respected (<=0.4):\", np.all(projected_w <= 0.40 + 1e-6))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Step through environment\n",
        "test_env = PortfolioEnv(market_split=splits.train)\n",
        "obs, info = test_env.reset()\n",
        "print(f\"\\nObservation Space Dimension: {test_env.observation_space.shape[0]}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Action Space Dimension:      {test_env.action_space.shape[0]}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "obs, reward, term, trunc, info = test_env.step(extreme_action)\n",
        "print(f\"Step 1 Executed: Turnover={info['turnover']:.4f}, Cost=${info['transaction_cost']:.2f}, Portfolio Value=${info['portfolio_value']:,.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. PPO Actor-Critic Policy Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "The Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) agent utilizes a decoupled Actor-Critic Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP):\n",
        "- **Actor Network (Policy Head)**: Maps the 52-dimensional state vector (45 market indicators + 5 current weights + 2 portfolio state metrics) through $[128, 128]$ Tanh layers to output continuous action scores for each asset.\n",
        "- **Critic Network (Value Head)**: Maps the state vector through $[128, 128]$ Tanh layers to estimate expected future discounted cumulative reward $V(s)$.\n",
        "- **GAE (Generalized Advantage Estimation)**: $\\lambda = 0.95, \\gamma = 0.99$ balances bias and variance in advantage estimates.\n",
        "- **Clipped Surrogate Objective**: $\\epsilon = 0.20$ prevents destructively large policy updates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "trained_agent = load_ppo_agent(CONFIG.best_model_path)\n",
        "print(\"Trained PPO Actor-Critic Architecture:\")\n",
        "print(trained_agent.policy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Out-of-Sample Backtesting & Benchmark Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "We evaluate the trained PPO agent on 502 trading days of **completely unseen test data** (2023\u20132024).\n",
        "We compare against four benchmark strategies under identical initial capital ($100,000), identical dates, and realistic proportional transaction costs:\n",
        "1. **PPO Actor-Critic (Rebalance AI)**: Dynamic daily allocation policy.\n",
        "2. **Equal Weight (1/N Rebalanced)**: 20% target each asset, rebalanced daily with transaction costs.\n",
        "3. **Buy-and-Hold (1/N Unrebalanced)**: Initial 20% each asset, free drift, zero rebalancing costs.\n",
        "4. **SPY Buy-and-Hold**: 100% S&P 500 benchmark.\n",
        "5. **60/40 Benchmark**: 60% SPY / 40% TLT rebalanced daily."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "engine = BacktestEngine(splits=splits, model_path=CONFIG.best_model_path)\n",
        "results = engine.run_full_evaluation()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\"*90)\n",
        "print(\"                OUT-OF-SAMPLE PERFORMANCE COMPARISON (2023-2024)\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*90)\n",
        "display(results[\"comparison_table\"].round(4))\n",
        "print(\"=\"*90)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Comprehensive Visualizations & Financial Risk Analysis"
      ]
