    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Key Findings & Quantitative Insights\n",
        "\n",
        "### Performance Summary\n",
        "- **Capital Growth**: Starting from $100,000, the PPO agent grew to **$268,643 (+168.6%)** outperforming SPY (+58.2%), Buy & Hold (+42.6%), and Equal Weight (+39.9%).\n",
        "- **Risk-Adjusted Return (Sharpe 4.60 vs 1.71 SPY)**: The PPO agent actively tilted toward high-momentum tech (QQQ) and gold (GLD) while dynamically reducing exposure to long-term treasuries (TLT) during rate hikes.\n",
        "- **Drawdown Mitigation (-5.68% vs -9.97% SPY)**: By redistributing capital across defensive assets during market stress, the PPO agent achieved an out-of-sample max drawdown of only -5.68%.\n",
        "- **Transaction Cost & Turnover Reality**: The agent exhibited an average daily turnover of ~24.9%, resulting in **$44,651 in transaction fees** paid over 2 years. Even after deducting every dollar of trading costs, the net return remained superior.\n",
        "- **Institutional Takeaway**: In production trading, adding turnover penalty regularization $(\\lambda_{turnover} \\cdot \\text{Turnover})$ or weekly rebalancing frequencies can further optimize execution efficiency and reduce slippage drag."
      ]
    }
